WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:04.760
Irene Palmer was born March 2nd, 1930 in&nbsp;
Bridgeport, Connecticut, as we can see right here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:09.280
on her passport. Irene’s mom was deeply religious,&nbsp;
claiming that God spoke to her directly.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:12.040
As a girl, Irene had a series&nbsp;
of visions just like her mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:15.120
but her father never believed any of&nbsp;
this. He thought his wife was crazy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:18.660
and had her committed to a psychiatric&nbsp;
hospital, forcing a tearful goodbye.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.480
–[Mother] I will always be with you.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.680
That was the last she ever saw of her mom, but&nbsp;
her visions continued, which created issues with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:28.400
her father. After each vision, Irene would&nbsp;
be left with the same thought in her head:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.960
“Mary points the way.” Word of her visions&nbsp;
eventually reached the Catholic Church, and they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:36.120
sent a Bishop to meet with the family and convince&nbsp;
her father not to have her committed as well.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:40.200
The script for The Nun offers a little more&nbsp;
insight. Scripts are not usually considered canon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.040
but this is one of those cases where&nbsp;
it’s relatively non-contradictory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:47.120
and even fits pretty well with The Nun&nbsp;
II, so I do want to talk about it briefly.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.640
Irene was investigated by the church to see if&nbsp;
she had potentially been possessed, but it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:55.200
ultimately decided that she was pure. The Bishop&nbsp;
suggested she dedicate her life to the Lord,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.000
and when she did so, her visions stopped, so&nbsp;
she planned to become a nun when she reached the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.440
proper age. And this process is sped up when Irene&nbsp;
is sent away to live in Europe by her father.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:08.960
–[Irene] I was different. Sending me away was&nbsp;
easier than trying to understand who I was.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:12.080
So she was born in Bridgeport,&nbsp;
Connecticut, has psychic visions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.560
and became connected to the Catholic Church?&nbsp;
If you follow The Conjuring franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:19.120
this should all sound similar to another&nbsp;
character: the paranormal investigator&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:23.200
slash basically superhero: Lorraine&nbsp;Warren. 
So what is the deal here?&nbsp;

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:26.760
 What&nbsp; is the true relationship between these&nbsp;
two characters? To answer that question,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:31.517
and to hear my full analysis of Sister&nbsp;
Irene, stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:31.517 --> 00:01:37.600
♪ Metal Music ♪

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:42.040
Welcome to Horror History. Yes, I have conjured&nbsp;
up another one from the Conjuring universe. As&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:45.520
the highest grossing horror franchise of all&nbsp;
time, The Conjuring films have done a great job&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:49.720
of incorporating familiar elements to keep people&nbsp;
interested in the spin-offs. The Annabelle doll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:53.360
was introduced in the first movie and became&nbsp;
the centerpiece of several films of her own,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:57.120
but for The Nun spin-off series, the&nbsp;
antagonist was not the only familiar element.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:00.920
In April 2017, it was announced that&nbsp;
Taissa Farmiga had been cast to play&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:04.320
the lead role. Taissa is the sister&nbsp;
of Vera Farmiga, who plays Lorraine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:07.960
Warren in the mainline Conjuring films.&nbsp;
So fans immediately began speculating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:11.600
that she could be related to Lorraine, or&nbsp;
possibly even be a younger version of her.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.880
Now, the last time I said the word titular in a&nbsp;
video, I pronounced it wrong. I said tight-ular,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:19.800
and everybody just eviscerated me in the comments.&nbsp;
And I just wanted to defend myself, because the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:24.040
word refers to the title of a work. So in my&nbsp;
mind it makes sense that it would be tight-ular.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:29.120
Like title. But I admit I was wrong. I think next&nbsp;
time I’ll just play it safe and say: e-pony-mous.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:33.320
Reason I bring this up is this Variety article&nbsp;
claims the younger Farmiga sister is playing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:37.920
titular role in the Nun. And I think that’s&nbsp;
kind of arguable. Yes, she does play a nun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.920
(or at least she becomes a nun) but when I hear&nbsp;
the title: The Nun, I’m not thinking about her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:46.760
I’m thinking about the nun demon: Valak. I don’t&nbsp;
think anyone would go see a Nun movie if Valak was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:50.680
not in it, but they would probably be just fine&nbsp;
if they did one without Sister Irene. But that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:55.160
being said, I would prefer to see more of this&nbsp;
character, not less. It would be fun to see her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:59.160
up against another villain in a different spin-off&nbsp;
series at some point. Because her backstory is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:03.840
mostly left as a mystery, other than a few clues&nbsp;
here and there. So to begin unraveling them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:07.416
let’s take it back to the unexpected&nbsp;
guest who changed the course of her life.

00:03:07.416 --> 00:03:10.000
(IMPACT)

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.191
♪ Dreadful Music ♪

00:03:13.191 --> 00:03:16.440
As an adult, Sister Irene works at&nbsp;
Saint Vincent Hospital in London,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:19.840
England. She still plans on becoming&nbsp;
a nun but hasn’t taken her vows yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:23.360
making her a novitiate. Something that&nbsp;
everyone likes to point out, constantly.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:30.600
[Montage of every time she’s asked about her vows]

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:35.480
Now you know how I feel everytime someone asks&nbsp;
me to make a Nun 2 video. I’M LITERALLY DOING IT.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:38.640
Different cultures handle it differently,&nbsp;
but there are basically 3 steps to becoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.920
a nun. First there’s Discernment. That’s where&nbsp;
you’re considered a “Sister” or “novitiate”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:47.000
but not yet a nun. Once a sister takes&nbsp;
her temporary vows, she becomes a nun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.200
and this kind of allows her to test&nbsp;
the lifestyle, and if she’s successful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.760
she may make her perpetual vows,&nbsp;
signifying lifelong commitment.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:58.580
In 1952, she’s a natural history teacher for&nbsp;
a group of kids who are in maybe fourth grade.

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:03.880
–[Irene] I have survived many terrifying encounters.&nbsp;
But nothing could have ever prepared me for&nbsp;this.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:15.040
My only hope was that the beast could not&nbsp;
smell me. But then, the wind changed and… ROAR!

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:18.480
This may just be a fictional story that she’s&nbsp;
telling to these kids to entertain them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.600
but it could also be a personal story&nbsp;
about her experiences growing up with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:25.480
supernatural visions. It’s possible that&nbsp;
she’s already taken on an entity in her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:29.080
past. If she grew up alongside Lorraine&nbsp;
Warren, then I would say it’s very likely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:31.917
since we know Lorraine also&nbsp;
had visions from a young age.

00:04:31.917 --> 00:04:34.080
–[Lorraine] You know, when I was about your age, um,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:38.320
I was visiting my mom at a hospital and&nbsp;
I saw an angel. It was standing next to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:43.000
a little boy's bed. It was just gently&nbsp;
touching his cheek and then it stopped.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:46.840
By the way, if Irene and Lorraine grew up&nbsp;
together, which they most likely did given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:52.040
that Lorraine was born in 1927 and Irene was&nbsp;
born in 1930, they are most likely cousins. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:56.600
know they aren’t sisters because Lorraine’s mom&nbsp;
is still around in old age, but Irene’s is not.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:00.200
Her dedication to religion made her believe&nbsp;
that anything could be a sign from God,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:04.040
such as her brushing red paint onto this&nbsp;
girl’s nose. We’ll come back to that.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:06.240
She’s visited by a representative of the Vatican,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:10.040
which is basically like the HQ of the&nbsp;
Catholic Church. His name is Father Burke,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:13.040
and she learns that she’s been assigned&nbsp;
to assist him on an investigation of an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:17.431
unusual phenomenon in Biertan, Romania,&nbsp;
due to her familiarity with the territory.

00:05:17.431 --> 00:05:20.880
–[Father Burke] Romania.
–[Irene] I’ve never been in that part of the world.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:24.640
Perhaps she’s been chosen, not because she is&nbsp;
geographically familiar, but rather because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:29.360
she’s familiar with the territory of supernatural&nbsp;
encounters, maybe even involving evil entities.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:33.040
This begs the question, why would they&nbsp;
choose her over Lorraine? Afterall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:36.840
this was the same year Lorraine founded the&nbsp;
New England Society for Psychic Research…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:40.720
at least in real life. It seems Irene was&nbsp;
chosen because of the nature of the mission.

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:44.880
Father Burke was to bring her to the Abbey of St.&nbsp;
Carta to determine if the grounds were still holy.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:49.920
–[Cardinal Conroy] Since it is a cloistered convent&nbsp;
and your access will be limited.

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:52.840
This basically means they are giving him&nbsp;
a guide because the church is cut off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:55.320
from the outside world. Given&nbsp;
that she’s a nun in training,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:59.120
she would be allowed to explore the inside&nbsp;
more than a normal civilian like Lorraine.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:03.951
But after arriving in Romania, things would&nbsp;
prove more difficult than anticipated.

00:06:03.951 --> 00:06:06.710
(IMPACT)

00:06:09.347 --> 00:06:13.054
♪ Suspenseful Music ♪

00:06:13.054 --> 00:06:16.480
Their first stop in Romania is to visit&nbsp;
Maurice Theriault, commonly known as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:20.680
Frenchie. He’s immediately flirting with her until&nbsp;
learning that she’s a prospective nun. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:23.840
she still charms him enough to convince&nbsp;
him to take them up to the abbey.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:25.159
-[Maurice] With all due respect father, I...

00:06:25.159 --> 00:06:28.380
–[Irene] Please, Frenchie.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:34.680
That was not that difficult. Don’t you have&nbsp;
anything better to do than simp? Once reaching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:38.280
the edge of the grounds, their horse refuses&nbsp;
to continue and they have to go by foot.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:41.880
This is just like the dog in the Conjuring, who&nbsp;
refused to enter the house haunted by the witch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:46.160
Bathsheba. They learn that the locals spit on the&nbsp;
ground when the topic of the abbey is brought up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:49.520
and the crosses lining the perimeter&nbsp;
may be keeping the evil locked in.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:53.600
They visit the ice house to check on the body&nbsp;
of the nun who killed herself, Sister Victoria,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:57.080
and she’s strangely been moved into an&nbsp;
upright position. Burke discovers a key&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.080 --> 00:07:00.560
clenched in her hands, and they decide&nbsp;
to give her a proper burial outside.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:05.200
Sister Irene begins to notice a number of strange&nbsp;
things. The blood at the site of Victoria’s death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:09.840
is still fresh, and upon entering the abbey she&nbsp;
senses something behind her without looking.

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:12.720
This appears to be the Reverend&nbsp;
Mother, or essentially the head Nun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:15.920
but what they don’t know is that&nbsp;
this is actually Valak, the defiler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:19.320
an ancient demon who is responsible&nbsp;
for the evil plaguing the Abbey.

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:22.200
Quick Horror History lesson for those&nbsp;
who haven't seen my Valak episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:25.800
this creature escaped from hell and killed off&nbsp;
each of the nuns at the abbey. Their spirits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:29.400
continue to inhabit the place as ghosts, but&nbsp;
the Reverend Mother’s ghost is under Valak’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:32.720
control. Much like how Bill Wilkins’s&nbsp;
ghost was controlled in The Conjuring 2.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:36.640
They're asked to come back in the morning, since&nbsp;
the sisters take a vow of silence after sunset.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:40.640
I bet my neighbors wish I would take a vow of&nbsp;
silence after sunset, but hey, that’s the best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:45.200
time to record videos. But Sister Irene and&nbsp;
Father Burke nearly don't make it to sunrise.

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:48.760
Burke gets trapped in a coffin by Valak,&nbsp;
and Irene is awoken by a breeze in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:52.360
middle of her sleep. If her visions are&nbsp;
believed to be messages sent to her by God,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:55.560
I don't think it's that crazy to assume&nbsp;
this was God waking her up so that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:58.920
could save her comrade, and stand&nbsp;
a chance to defeat Valak later on.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:01.560
She comes upon some kind of&nbsp;
midnight ritual in a chapel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:06.240
where Valak appears to her as a shadow, but after&nbsp;
she realizes the ritual was all an apparition;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:09.117
and the demonic entity makes&nbsp;
itself known in a bold way.

00:08:09.267 --> 00:08:12.920
(roar) (mirror shatter)

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:17.200
The fact that Sister Irene sees Valak in its&nbsp;
nun form in the mirror has to be symbolic of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:21.400
choice that lies ahead of her. She’s considering&nbsp;
becoming a Nun herself, but struggles to make the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:25.880
commitment to take her vows. It’s almost as if&nbsp;
Valak in the mirror represents her fears about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:30.200
her potential future, a theme that would come up&nbsp;
throughout her story. She’s also not the only one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:34.920
to encounter Valak in this way, this is another&nbsp;
connection Sister Irene shares with Lorraine.

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:39.040
Also in the nearby town, they have a tradition&nbsp;
to cover their mirrors whenever someone dies

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:41.600
–[Irene] …so the deceased doesn’t see their&nbsp;reflection.

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:43.600
This is likely why Valak destroyed the mirror,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:47.040
so that Irene can never find out that&nbsp;
all of the nuns are already dead.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:51.080
After fleeing the chapel, she hears a bell ringing&nbsp;
and instantly knows Father Burke is in trouble.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:55.160
The gravesites around the perimeter contain what&nbsp;
are known as safety coffins. The bell system was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.160 --> 00:09:00.120
developed in 1892, with strings connecting the&nbsp;
occupants head, hands and feet to a bell on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:04.120
outside. This way, the cemetery watchman would be&nbsp;
alerted if they accidentally buried a live one.

00:09:04.760 --> 00:09:07.760
If you’re wondering if this is where the&nbsp;
phrase “Saved by the Bell” comes from,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:10.960
it’s not, according to this article&nbsp;
from Ripley’s Believe It Or Not.

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:14.360
But apparently the phrase doesn’t come&nbsp;
from school either, it comes from boxing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:17.720
and as someone who shares a name with the&nbsp;
main character from a cultural touchstone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:21.120
sitcom called Saved by the Bell,&nbsp;
YOU WOULD THINK I WOULD KNOW THAT.

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:24.240
Anyway, Sister Irene had learned&nbsp;
about safety coffins earlier that day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:27.960
and somehow knew the Father was in trouble&nbsp;
when she heard one ringing. As she got close,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:30.360
Valak chimed all of the bells&nbsp;
in order to confuse her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:35.198
and we see her close her eyes and envision&nbsp;
which distress call is the real deal.

00:09:35.198 --> 00:09:36.840
(breath shutters as she comes out of trance)

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:40.360
The next day, he sends Irene away with&nbsp;
the key acquired from Sister Victoria’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:44.680
cold dead fingers. I bet he tells that story,&nbsp;
seriously like whenever he gets the chance.

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:54.080
“And then… I pried the key from her cold&nbsp;
dead hands. Waiter, one more round please.”

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:58.080
Sister Irene finds the main sanctuary and&nbsp;
comes across Sister Oana, who informs her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:01.180
that the nuns are taking prayer shifts&nbsp;
to maintain a constant state of prayer.

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:06.200
–[Oana] Sister Victoria’s death was a&nbsp;
terrible tragedy for the convent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:11.120
but we still feel her presence. She&nbsp;
was the most devoted out of any of us…

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:14.100
Has anyone else noticed that we are&nbsp;
literally getting Shyamalonged right now?

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:15.800
–[Cole Sear] They don’t know they’re dead…

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:19.280
Personally, I’m never one to complain&nbsp;
about getting Shyamalonged or Weezered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:22.000
or Rick Rolled or even Josh&nbsp;
Hutcherson Whistle Edited!

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:25.502
(Josh Hutcherson whistle edit)

00:10:25.502 --> 00:10:29.960
They also discuss an imposter nun which&nbsp;
sister Oana describes as something unholy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:34.280
perhaps the evil re-emerging after being&nbsp;
sealed so many years. Another sister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:38.160
Sister Abigail, instructs Sister Oana&nbsp;
to resume her prayers, and tells Irene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:43.280
that she should not be here since she has not&nbsp;
taken her vows yet. We f*cking get itttttt!!!

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:46.160
However, she’s told she has to stay the&nbsp;
night, because the gates have once again&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:49.680
closed until morning. My theory about the&nbsp;
mirrors being connected to Irene’s fear of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:53.240
becoming a Nun is supported here, because&nbsp;
the room she stays in contains a mirror,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:56.880
and she receives another vision in her dream,&nbsp;
where “Mary points the way” echoes through her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:01.640
head and she envisions Valak, the suicide of&nbsp;
Sister Victoria, and a girl covered in blood.

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:06.360
When she awakens, a door opens and she’s beckoned&nbsp;
to explore by a spectral voice, leading to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:11.360
discovery of an underground passage marked by the&nbsp;
words “Finit hic Deo”, Latin for “God Ends Here”.

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:15.760
It opens to reveal the bane of all things&nbsp;
holy: Valak. She finds herself suddenly in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:19.480
a windstorm as she tries to escape, but&nbsp;
the evil Nun just grins menacingly at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:23.193
her. It comes to a halt as she’s slammed&nbsp;
into the door, but then, this happens.

00:11:23.425 --> 00:11:25.461
(hands come out and grab her)

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:28.200
What little light there is in&nbsp;
the corridor is smothered away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:31.680
and she’s pulled into a hiding spot by&nbsp;
Sister Oana. When the threat passes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:34.520
she’s instructed to get her things and&nbsp;
meet in the chapel so that they can pray&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:39.537
their way through the night. But after arriving&nbsp;
there, Sister Irene makes a gruesome discovery.

00:11:39.537 --> 00:11:42.873
(IMPACT)

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:48.754
♪ Suspenseful Music ♪

00:11:48.754 --> 00:11:53.080
In the main sanctuary, Irene finds a nun praying&nbsp;fervently next to a body under a sheet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:56.840
which turns out to be Sister Oana.&nbsp;
A whole flock of nuns storms in. I’m&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:59.520
pretty sure I established in a previous&nbsp;
video that at some point that a group of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:02.320
nuns traveling together like this&nbsp;
should be referred to as a flock,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:06.440
and I’m sticking with it. They lock the place up,&nbsp;
and sister Ruth urges Irene to pray with them.

00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:09.320
–[Ruth] And whatever happens,&nbsp;
whatever you may see or hear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:11.880
keep your eyes forward, and don’t stop praying.

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:17.000
Sister Irene hyperventilates, but compiles.&nbsp;
Suddenly, a blast AIR YEETS all the other nuns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:20.640
away from her, and she does exactly&nbsp;
what sister Ruth told her *not* to,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:24.040
she diverts her eyes and her prayer&nbsp;
is interrupted. This whole scene is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:28.410
another test of her commitment to religion on her&nbsp;
journey to becoming a nun. By looking away, she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:33.240
is distracted by outside elements. But then she&nbsp;
refocuses her attention and continues her prayer.

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:37.800
Her garb is then ripped open from behind, but&nbsp;
this is not Frenchie choosing an inopportune&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:42.680
time to make his move, it is instead, an invisible&nbsp;
force that scratches a pentagram into her back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:46.720
This is another test of her dedication, she&nbsp;
must tune out the pain to continue her prayer.

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:49.700
It’s like when you’re trying to get work&nbsp;
done, but you see the notification that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:52.720
CZsWorld just uploaded, and you have&nbsp;
to resist the temptation to watch the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:56.560
video. Except in that scenario, the&nbsp;
correct answer is to watch the video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.560 --> 00:13:00.560
or at least put it on in the background, but my&nbsp;
point is that her restraint was being tested.

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:03.760
She only stops when she hears Father&nbsp;
Burke and Frenchie trying to get in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:06.040
and one of the other nuns&nbsp;
gives her a nod of approval.

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:09.400
After letting them in, she tells them that&nbsp;
they’ve all been praying to hold back the evil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:13.320
but when she turns back, all of the others&nbsp;
are gone. And this is what makes her realize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:16.920
that the “nuns” she’s been seeing up until&nbsp;
this point were just part of her visions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:20.360
or rather, spirits of the deceased&nbsp;
nuns that once inhabited the abbey.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:23.040
In other words, there was&nbsp;
nobody left when they arrived,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:27.093
the place is filled with ghosts.&nbsp;
And apparently reanimated corpses.

00:13:27.093 --> 00:13:30.520
(growls and screams)

00:13:30.520 --> 00:13:34.080
He instructs her to get some holy water from&nbsp;
his bag and throw it on the evil nun. And I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:37.840
love in all these movies whenever they try to&nbsp;
make the priests these badass action heroes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:41.280
and they just have their satchels packed with holy&nbsp;
water so they can just whip it out like a gun.

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:44.840
And it works. It works every time.&nbsp;
He douses a cross in holy water and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:47.360
uses it to drive the demonic&nbsp;
force out of the nun’s body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:51.720
which goes up in flames when the entity can no&nbsp;
longer endure the divinity bearing down on it.

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:54.680
Frenchie’s about ready to GTFO, but Sister Irene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:58.200
bravely insists they cannot leave without&nbsp;
first sealing the gateway to contain the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:02.960
evil. She’s come a long way. At first she had&nbsp;
no idea what her purpose was on this mission,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:06.600
but now, she’s the one leading the charge&nbsp;
into the underground passages to search for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:11.240
the blood of Christ that will supposedly send the&nbsp;
crooked-nose conventual back where it came from.

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:15.360
And having found her purpose, she’s ready to&nbsp;
make a commitment she wasn’t sure about before.

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:17.040
– I’d like to take my vows.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:20.880
She does this because she discovered her&nbsp;
visions are a miracle of God. Either that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:24.952
or she’s just sick of everyone asking her about&nbsp;
it. It’s kind of an L for Frenchie though.

00:14:24.952 --> 00:14:28.200
–[Frenchie] Now that, Sister, is a&nbsp;
noble act. It’s a shame, but…

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:32.520
Oh Frenchie. You’ll find someone.&nbsp;
Briefly. Then you’ll die. Imagine if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:35.320
you were crushing on a girl, and then&nbsp;
she became a nun and swore herself to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:35.320 --> 00:14:38.760
celibacy. That’s kinda like… I don’t&nbsp;
know, I think I’d be kinda salty.

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:42.760
Father Burke helps her make what I believe&nbsp;
are her temporary vows. And she’s t-posing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:46.120
face down on the ground, so that’s kinda&nbsp;
funny. After officially becoming a nun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:48.880
she feels she’s ready to face&nbsp;
down the demon posing as a nun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:52.000
no longer willing to be taunted by&nbsp;
the form that she felt mocked by.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:55.880
In the corridors under the Abbey, a beam&nbsp;
of Light shines down on the finger of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:55.880 --> 00:15:00.000
Virgin Mary statue, connecting to the phrase&nbsp;
associated with her visions since childhood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:03.960
“Mary points the way” and further making&nbsp;
her believe that her visions came from God.

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:09.280
They follow the beam to a secret keyhole in&nbsp;
the wall, and unlock it to find the glass&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:12.560
orb containing the blood of Christ,&nbsp;
and Father Burke tells her that only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:16.360
a true bride of Christ can wield it. So I&nbsp;
guess it’s a good thing she did the vows.

00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:20.480
With the ultimate weapon in hand, they proceed&nbsp;
past the cellar door for the first time into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:24.640
area where evil reigns supreme. They split&nbsp;
up, you know, the thing you’re definitely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:28.640
supposed to do in a horror movie, and Irene&nbsp;
is stalked by a faceless nun as she hears the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:28.640 --> 00:15:32.280
whispers of the spirits of the nuns who had&nbsp;
assisted her, but before she can do anything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:36.440
she’s chokeslammed by Valak, and runs to a&nbsp;
seemingly unused storage room for safety.

00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:40.680
Once again, there’s a mirror, and for the third&nbsp;
time now, it would be connected to Valak. She’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.680 --> 00:15:45.320
encircled by five candles which light themselves&nbsp;
and realizes she’s standing in a pentagram,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:49.360
but as she runs for the exit, she’s stopped&nbsp;
in her tracks by an army of robed figures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:52.920
who abduct her and bag her head,&nbsp;
forcing her to join their ranks.

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:55.800
Frenchie eventually finds her,&nbsp;
but when he uncovers her head,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:59.680
she’s been possessed by Valak, and she AIR&nbsp;
YEETS him into a pillar, which he’s pinned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:03.800
against. This is the next logical step in&nbsp;
the mirror metaphor. Valak had used mirrors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:08.280
to make Irene fear her future as a nun, and now&nbsp;
that she’s realized that life by becoming one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:11.720
Valak would literally possess her,&nbsp;
it’s bringing those fears to fruition.

00:16:11.720 --> 00:16:14.720
The possessed Irene hurls targeted&nbsp;
insults about Frenchie being the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:19.151
village idiot. It’s a trope we’ve seen a lot in&nbsp;
the exorcism genre, going back to the Exorcist.

00:16:19.151 --> 00:16:23.560
However, he’s able to use the vial hanging from&nbsp;
her neck to smear the blood of Christ on her face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:27.400
calling back to the beginning of the adventure&nbsp;
when she smeared paint on the girl’s nose.

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:29.600
This has an immediate and powerful effect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:32.640
exorcizing the demon from her body.&nbsp;
And it’s honestly just nice to see an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:36.680
exorcism scene in this franchise that doesn’t&nbsp;
involve throwing up that black substance.

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:40.560
She’s knocked aside as Valak deviously&nbsp;
grabs Frenchie by the throat and flashes a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:44.740
disgusting smile in her direction. She tries&nbsp;
to bum rush the evil entity, but she’s AIR&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:44.740 --> 00:16:48.960
YEETED completely out of the room into a pool of&nbsp;
water that’s formed by flooding from overhead.

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:52.880
It’s possible that this moment is supposed&nbsp;
to represent a symbolic baptism. A baptism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:57.480
is a Christian practice of submerging a person in&nbsp;
water to cleanse or purify them as an initiation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:57.480 --> 00:17:01.680
to joining the religion. This is more of a&nbsp;
symbolic baptism than a literal one. Being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:05.720
baptized is a requirement for being a catholic&nbsp;
nun, so it’s likely that Sister Irene already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:05.720 --> 00:17:08.880
went through the baptism ceremony when&nbsp;
she was young. But now that she’s taken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:12.840
her vows and joined the sisterhood of nuns,&nbsp;
she’s starting a new chapter of her life.

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:17.280
On the website tv tropes, a symbolic baptism&nbsp;
is defined as “a sign of character development&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:20.760
where swimming or watery immersion marks&nbsp;
a major turning point in the characters'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:24.360
life. Most commonly, it marks the point where&nbsp;
the character begins to let go of the past,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:24.360 --> 00:17:26.680
or is initiated into a new phase of their life”.

00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:30.400
So this fits Sister Irene pretty well.&nbsp;
She loses grasp of the holy grail,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:35.245
but when she goes to reach for it, she notices&nbsp;
Valak rising up from below the surface.

00:17:35.245 --> 00:17:38.121
(IMPACT)

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:44.465
♪ Intense Music ♪

00:17:44.465 --> 00:17:47.760
Valak attacks, and holds down Sister&nbsp;
Irene under the water. Even Father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:51.200
Burke’s prayers do little to slow it&nbsp;
down. However, he does provide just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:54.840
enough of a distraction for Irene to bring&nbsp;
the grail to her mouth under the surface.

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:57.880
With that, Valak believes that it has&nbsp;
won and lifts her up to eye level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:57.880 --> 00:18:01.520
but realizes the contents of the&nbsp;
glass case has been removed. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:05.000
Irene outsmarts her hellish counterpart&nbsp;
with where she’s hidden the goods.

00:18:05.622 --> 00:18:09.375
(spits on Valak)

00:18:09.375 --> 00:18:13.640
For years, the people in town have spit on the&nbsp;
ground after any mention of the evil as an ancient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:13.640 --> 00:18:18.360
superstition, and now Irene is using that same&nbsp;
tactic to hopefully finish it off for good.

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:20.120
And this has a devastating effect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:24.200
as Valak appears to be sucked down into&nbsp;
a vortex and back where it came from.

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:27.754
Before leaving, she gives a proper&nbsp;
blessing to the nuns of St. Carta.

00:18:27.754 --> 00:18:30.880
–[Frenchie] I thought this ground wasn’t holy anymore.
–[Irene} It is now.

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:33.720
Before leaving Romania, she sees&nbsp;
off Frenchie at the train station,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:37.320
and learns he’s planning on going to&nbsp;
Hungary, then traveling the world.

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:41.280
At some point after this, she must have gone back&nbsp;
to the Vatican with Father Burke, and met Cardinal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:45.280
Conroy, who was obviously impressed enough by&nbsp;
her work to call upon her again in the future.

00:18:45.280 --> 00:18:49.540
The story of what happened in Romania becomes kind&nbsp;
of an urban legend among other sisters and nuns.

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:53.120
–[Nun] What happened to the nun?
–[Sister Jessica] Well, no one really knows.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:59.120
They say the experience was too much&nbsp;
for her. Some say that she went mad.

00:18:59.120 --> 00:19:03.320
It seems like it would be difficult for gossip to&nbsp;
spread, considering cloistered nuns generally do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:03.320 --> 00:19:07.760
not travel, however other nuns and sisters&nbsp;
do apparently travel a lot. Primarily for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:07.760 --> 00:19:11.280
missionary work, where they try to recruit&nbsp;
people in other countries to their religion.

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:15.640
They would not be the only ones bothering people&nbsp;
from other countries. After lying dormant inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:15.640 --> 00:19:22.280
of Frenchie for 4 years, Valak would re-emerge in&nbsp;
1955 and 1956 and take four victims across Europe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:25.960
one of which was a priest named Father Noiret&nbsp;
(no-are-ayy) who was immolated at his church&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:25.960 --> 00:19:30.400
in Tarascon, France. Because of course the&nbsp;
French priest would be named after wine.

00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:34.000
That night, Irene wakes up in the middle&nbsp;
of the night in a manner very similar to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:37.520
when the breeze woke her up at St. Carta’s,&nbsp;
right down to the way the curtain blows in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:37.520 --> 00:19:42.320
breeze. Given my earlier analysis, I would&nbsp;
interpret this as a divine call to action.

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:44.120
And in fact, this is another dream,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:47.560
a vision of Maurice possessed by&nbsp;
Valak, and asking to be saved.

00:19:47.560 --> 00:19:51.440
The next day she’s visited by Cardinal&nbsp;
Conroy. She doesn’t look thrilled to see him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:55.340
which is kinda understandable considering&nbsp;
this dude only shows up to deliver bad news.

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:57.240
–[Father Conroy] There has been an incident.

00:19:57.240 --> 00:20:01.760
See? I told you! He doesn’t even make any&nbsp;
small talk first… I am the exact same way.

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:05.000
She’s given the lowdown on the four&nbsp;
gruesome deaths moving west across Europe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:07.600
which they suspect to be the work of&nbsp;
the demon she thought she had sealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:10.820
away 4 years prior with the help&nbsp;
of Father Burke. Speaking of whom.

00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:12.600
–[Father Conroy] Father Burke is dead.

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:17.280
See, this guy never has good news. She doesn’t&nbsp;
want to go, but they basically strong-arm her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:17.280 --> 00:20:20.960
Luckily, her friend Sister Debra tags along&nbsp;
to look after her, so she’s not completely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:20.960 --> 00:20:25.440
solo as she begins her search at the site of&nbsp;
the last known incident: Tarascon, France.

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:29.200
Like the Abbey in Romania, there’s a belief&nbsp;
that this church is cursed following Valak’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:32.680
appearance. As she looks around the place,&nbsp;
she’s able to see visions of the past:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:37.440
falling ash, the burnt up husk of Father&nbsp;
Noiret and the boy who inherited his rosary.

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:39.360
They’re taken to see Father Noiret’s room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:39.360 --> 00:20:42.800
where they come across a picture of&nbsp;
St. Lucy, Patron Saint of the Blind.

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:46.360
Like much of the lore in the Conjurverse,&nbsp;
St. Lucy is based on a real person,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:46.360 --> 00:20:51.200
a saint from Italy in the 200s who devoted herself&nbsp;
to Christianity. There are a number of myths and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:51.200 --> 00:20:55.040
stories about the cause of her blindness.&nbsp;
Some versions say she gouged out her own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:55.040 --> 00:20:59.000
eyes when a potential lover became infatuated&nbsp;
with them, in order to prove her dedication to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:02.600
religion and virginity. Another take on the&nbsp;
matter tells of how she was captured by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:02.600 --> 00:21:06.800
Roman Emperor Diocletian (die-uh-klee-shin), and&nbsp;
her eyes were gouged out prior to her execution.

00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:09.780
That seems to be closer to version of&nbsp;
the tale that appears in the Conjurverse.

00:21:09.780 --> 00:21:13.360
–[Irene] She was murdered by pagans. They&nbsp;
lit her on fire but she wouldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:13.360 --> 00:21:16.120
burn. Before killing her they gouged out her eyes.

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:20.120
Very metal. Irene learns that Frenchie had&nbsp;
worked at this very church as a handyman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:23.520
until Father Noiret was killed, and&nbsp;
comes to the realization pretty quickly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:23.520 --> 00:21:26.720
that *he* must have been the vessel&nbsp;
that smuggled Valak out of the Abbey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:30.320
and the reason these tragedies are&nbsp;
seemingly spreading across the continent.

00:21:30.320 --> 00:21:34.680
While checking in at the Hotel Tarascon, Irene’s&nbsp;
sixth sense is on high alert and she’s led out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:38.640
into the street where she sees the alter boy,&nbsp;
Jacques, among a group of kids playing European&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:38.640 --> 00:21:42.360
football. Jacques is the one whose father&nbsp;
was killed by Valak. In pursuit of answers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:46.400
she finds herself at a newstand, where the wind&nbsp;
blows the pages of each magazine open to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:51.040
right page to collectively form the haunting image&nbsp;
of Valak, right next to this picture of Harambe.

00:21:51.040 --> 00:21:54.600
When she gets close to it, Valak&nbsp;
appears in a flash and grabs her throat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:58.040
and in this instant, she receives a&nbsp;
vision of a burning ritual in a forest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:01.960
where a man in a red cloak stabs a nun in&nbsp;
the face as she holds some kind of artifact.

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:05.080
He stabs her twice, then we see a&nbsp;
divine light coming from her eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:05.080 --> 00:22:09.520
leading me to believe this is a representation&nbsp;
of St. Lucy, Patron Saint of the Blind.

00:22:09.520 --> 00:22:13.520
Irene passes out in the street, not waking up&nbsp;
until the next morning. I’m not sure if the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:18.340
doctor was using a figure of speech or if Irene’s&nbsp;
survival from this incident was not guaranteed.

00:22:18.340 --> 00:22:21.280
–[Doctor] There she is, back from ze dead.

00:22:21.280 --> 00:22:24.920
I kind of wish I could see what happened in&nbsp;
between. It seems like she was out for like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:24.920 --> 00:22:29.280
8 hours at least. Was the doctor just prodding her&nbsp;
and shining lights in her eyes all night until she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:29.280 --> 00:22:33.040
woke up? And then he just leaves without getting&nbsp;
paid? Are we sure this dude is a real doctor?

00:22:33.040 --> 00:22:34.840
–[Debra] What happened last night?

00:22:34.840 --> 00:22:36.834
Nah! That’s what she should be asking you! Anyway,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:36.834 --> 00:22:41.200
Irene concludes that Valak is using Frenchie&nbsp;
to get at this relic she saw in her vision.

00:22:41.200 --> 00:22:44.160
While she was unconscious, Jacques&nbsp;
visited Sister Debra and dropped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:44.160 --> 00:22:47.200
off his father’s rosary, which is&nbsp;
basically this necklace with a cross,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:47.200 --> 00:22:50.940
which is often seen being used to fend off&nbsp;
demons, and it also contains this symbol.

00:22:50.940 --> 00:22:54.840
–[Irene] This symbol seems so&nbsp;
familiar but I can’t place it.

00:22:54.840 --> 00:22:58.320
I’ll give her the benefit of the doubt and&nbsp;
just assume she’s still a little foggy since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:58.320 --> 00:23:01.560
she just woke up, but it’s clearly the&nbsp;
symbol from the artifact in her vision,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:05.360
which doesn’t seem like it was that long ago.&nbsp;
The symbol also matches a piece of jewelry seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:05.360 --> 00:23:09.680
in the crime scene photos of the other Valak&nbsp;
victims provided by Cardinal “Bad News” Conroy.

00:23:09.680 --> 00:23:13.240
They hurry to Palais de Papes (palay du Pop), the&nbsp;
Catholic archives, to try to learn what they can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:13.240 --> 00:23:17.293
about this symbol, but they would also receive&nbsp;
a tip that would have rippling ramifications.

00:23:17.293 --> 00:23:20.928
(IMPACT)

00:23:23.466 --> 00:23:26.646
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:23:26.646 --> 00:23:31.040
The librarian at the Catholic archives is able&nbsp;
to identify the symbol they brought in as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:31.040 --> 00:23:34.800
family crest of St. Lucy. The archivist&nbsp;
thinks each of the demon’s victims are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:34.800 --> 00:23:38.720
descendents of St. Lucy, and that Valak is&nbsp;
hunting them down in search of “The Eyes”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:38.720 --> 00:23:43.160
a sacred relic in Lucy’s family that holds&nbsp;
spiritual power, much like the blood of Christ.

00:23:43.160 --> 00:23:46.320
According to his records, he thinks they&nbsp;
can find the eyes buried at the monastery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:46.320 --> 00:23:49.920
of Jean Paul Redar, (roe-dar) which is now&nbsp;
a boarding school. They rush over there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:49.920 --> 00:23:52.560
hoping to arrive before the&nbsp;
relic falls into the wrong hands,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:52.560 --> 00:23:55.640
and the first person she encounters&nbsp;
is none other than her old guide,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:55.640 --> 00:24:00.620
Frenchie, but the reunion is soured by Irene’s&nbsp;
accusation that the evil is living inside of him.

00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:03.080
–[Irene] GET AWAY FROM THEM!

00:24:03.080 --> 00:24:08.400
– [Frenchie] What? We&nbsp;need to go… Now!
–[Irene] It’s you! It’s inside of you.

00:24:08.400 --> 00:24:13.000
This causes the dormant unholiness to take&nbsp;
over his body and deliver a chilling greeting.

00:24:13.000 --> 00:24:15.040
–[Valak] Hello sister.

00:24:15.040 --> 00:24:17.760
When she tries to follow him, he&nbsp;
right-hooks her into a window,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:17.760 --> 00:24:21.840
but she comes back with the rosary and commands&nbsp;
the demon to leave his body. Sister Deborah chips&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:21.840 --> 00:24:25.320
in with the Bellinger Bash, and they chain&nbsp;
up the unconscious Maurice in a hallway.

00:24:25.320 --> 00:24:28.680
–[Irene] He’s sick. We’re going to&nbsp;
help him, but we need your help.

00:24:28.680 --> 00:24:32.600
Sister Irene has serious Universal&nbsp;
Studios ride preshow energy right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:32.600 --> 00:24:35.800
here. Like how they always try to make the&nbsp;
rider feel like they’re a part of the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:35.800 --> 00:24:39.280
and then the “help” that we give is&nbsp;
literally just being along for the ride,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:39.280 --> 00:24:42.920
but when you get back to the station, everyone&nbsp;
claps for you like you’ve accomplished something.

00:24:42.920 --> 00:24:46.440
They realize that Frenchie was headed towards&nbsp;
the old haunted chapel, and the young boarding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:46.440 --> 00:24:50.120
student, Sophie, fills them in on the lore:&nbsp;
that the goat on this stained glass window is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:50.120 --> 00:24:53.240
a devil whose eyes will glow red when&nbsp;
the sun hits it at right right angle.

00:24:53.240 --> 00:24:56.840
They’re able to recreate this with a flashlight,&nbsp;
and find the end point of the red beam, which must&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:56.840 --> 00:25:00.880
be pointing out where the eyes of St. Lucy are&nbsp;
buried. If you’re getting a little bit of déjà vu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:00.880 --> 00:25:04.400
it’s probably because this is the exact&nbsp;
same puzzle as the one Irene solved back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:04.400 --> 00:25:07.920
at the Abbey of St. Carta to find the blood&nbsp;
of Christ, but this time instead of being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:07.920 --> 00:25:12.480
directed by a supposedly divine figure, she’s&nbsp;
following the clues of a supposedly demonic one.

00:25:12.480 --> 00:25:17.280
Is this representative of the potential danger&nbsp;
that lies in trying to use the eyes? A sign that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:17.280 --> 00:25:20.960
this time, they’re playing with a weapon&nbsp;
they may not be able to control? Maybe.

00:25:20.960 --> 00:25:24.280
The goat demon disappears from the stained&nbsp;
glass and appears in the girls’ sleeping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:24.280 --> 00:25:26.720
quarters on the other side of the&nbsp;
school, causing mayhem for them to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:26.720 --> 00:25:30.920
tend to. But they soon discover the reason this&nbsp;
previously inanimate object has come to life:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:30.920 --> 00:25:36.120
Frenchie has escaped from his chains under Valak’s&nbsp;
control, and AIR YEETS Sophie’s mom out of the way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:36.120 --> 00:25:40.800
on route to tackling Sister Irene, and forcing a&nbsp;
fumble which is recovered and advanced by Sophie.

00:25:40.800 --> 00:25:45.200
This does draw Frenchie-Valak’s attention away,&nbsp;
but Sister Irene is left in pretty bad shape.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:45.200 --> 00:25:49.440
There may be some symbolism here pertaining to&nbsp;
Irene’s own relationship with her father. There’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:49.440 --> 00:25:54.240
no mention of him being *physically* abusive to&nbsp;
her, but Irene says that she was sent away by him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:54.240 --> 00:25:58.280
because that was easier than trying to understand&nbsp;
her. Clearly, it’s a strained relationship.

00:25:58.280 --> 00:26:02.040
Frenchie has been trying to take on a fatherly&nbsp;
role himself lately, doing his best to serve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:02.040 --> 00:26:05.800
as a role model for Sophie before Sister&nbsp;
Irene showed up. So his attack on Sister&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:05.800 --> 00:26:10.160
Irene was likely received as a very personal&nbsp;
jab, given her problems with her own father.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:10.160 --> 00:26:14.320
It wouldn’t be that different from when Valak&nbsp;
temporarily possessed Sister Irene in 1952,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:14.320 --> 00:26:17.880
and started hurling targeted insults&nbsp;
about Frenchie being the village idiot.

00:26:17.880 --> 00:26:21.640
The extremely helpful archive librarian&nbsp;
guy even hinted that the demon of St.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:21.640 --> 00:26:23.820
Carta would choose its form to prey on her fears.

00:26:23.820 --> 00:26:29.560
–[Librarian] And the fears of those around you. You&nbsp;
must be prepared to stop it at all costs.

00:26:29.560 --> 00:26:33.240
That guy was such a king, by the way. He&nbsp;
basically solved the whole mystery for them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:33.240 --> 00:26:37.520
told them exactly where to go and what they would&nbsp;
be up against. And his name isn’t even mentioned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:37.520 --> 00:26:42.040
outside of the credits! Let’s give it up for&nbsp;
Father Ridley. The true hero of this story.

00:26:42.040 --> 00:26:45.120
Anyway, Irene is only able to track&nbsp;
down where Sophie and Frenchie-Valak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:45.120 --> 00:26:49.160
ran off to after seeing this tower start to&nbsp;
crumble under the power of St. Lucy’s eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:49.160 --> 00:26:53.440
which she uses to ward off the demon moments after&nbsp;
retrieving the blessed artifact from the Sophie.

00:26:53.440 --> 00:26:55.360
Her will is tested when Frenchie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:55.360 --> 00:26:59.080
what appears to be the real Frenchie,&nbsp;
gets through and begs for his life.

00:26:59.080 --> 00:27:02.800
–[Frenchie] Sister please. It’s killing me.

00:27:02.800 --> 00:27:07.600
But she knows she must not hold back in order to&nbsp;
prevent anyone else from becoming a victim. Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:07.600 --> 00:27:11.400
that’s what Father Ridley told her, and he’s&nbsp;
basically a God among men at this point.

00:27:11.400 --> 00:27:15.600
Just when it seems he’s finished, Frenchie-Valak&nbsp;
springs back to life and grabs the eyes from her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:15.600 --> 00:27:20.120
and seems to absorb them? And Valak&nbsp;
rises up -- in nun form -- behind him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:20.120 --> 00:27:21.880
now taking on an enormous stature.

00:27:21.880 --> 00:27:25.200
She tries using the rosary, but&nbsp;
that didn’t work in 1952 so why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:25.200 --> 00:27:28.560
would it work now? Valak responds by&nbsp;
shooting this chain at Sister Deborah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:28.560 --> 00:27:32.760
and Irene is levitated into the air in a&nbsp;
crucifixion pose and lit on fire. Valak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:32.760 --> 00:27:37.520
seems to be using the power of the eyes to deal&nbsp;
Irene the same fate that St. Lucy once suffered.

00:27:37.520 --> 00:27:41.920
But then, Irene experiences a quickflash&nbsp;
series of images, so let’s break them down.

00:27:41.920 --> 00:27:45.640
First she hears her mother’s words: “I&nbsp;
will always be with you.” Then she sees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:45.640 --> 00:27:48.880
her mother looking at her, followed by&nbsp;
two images of the burning of St. Lucy at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:48.880 --> 00:27:53.400
the hands of the pagans. Then the picture&nbsp;
of St. Lucy, from Father Noiret’s church.

00:27:53.400 --> 00:27:58.560
She also sees Valak standing in Lorraine Warren’s&nbsp;
home in 1977 -- and, intercut with more flashes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:58.560 --> 00:28:03.000
of her mom, an image of Loraine Warren opening&nbsp;
her eyes after seeing Valak for the first time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:03.000 --> 00:28:07.760
which also doesn’t happen until 1977. Not&nbsp;
the first example of her having future sight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:07.760 --> 00:28:11.040
but maybe the first time she gets a&nbsp;
glance into someone else’s future.

00:28:11.040 --> 00:28:13.640
After a few more images of the&nbsp;
attempted burning of St. Lucy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:13.640 --> 00:28:18.240
her own flame goes out and she falls to the&nbsp;
ground. Like St. Lucy, the pagan was unable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:18.240 --> 00:28:22.080
to burn her. And I’m considering Valak&nbsp;
to represent the Pagan in this instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:22.080 --> 00:28:26.160
because Valak’s lore comes from a grimoire, or&nbsp;
spellbook, called Ars Goetia, part of a series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:26.160 --> 00:28:29.800
of demon-summoning guide books called The&nbsp;
Lesser Key of Solomon. So the summoning of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:29.800 --> 00:28:34.280
Valak is not connected to any major religion,&nbsp;
thus making it a pagan mythological entity.

00:28:34.280 --> 00:28:38.240
So what do all of these images mean? Well,&nbsp;
remember back at the beginning when I suggested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:38.240 --> 00:28:42.600
that Irene and Lorraine probably have some blood&nbsp;
relation due to the actresses that portray them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:42.600 --> 00:28:46.640
Vera and Taissa Farmiga, being sisters?&nbsp;
Well, there is another pair of characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:46.640 --> 00:28:52.240
whose actresses share common blood. St. Lucy and&nbsp;
Irene’s mom are both played by Kate Colebrook,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:52.240 --> 00:28:56.760
which, to me, suggests that these characters&nbsp;
are supposed to be related as well. Meaning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:56.760 --> 00:29:01.360
that Irene and Lorraine are both part of the&nbsp;
bloodline of St. Lucy. Which means the images&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:01.360 --> 00:29:05.920
that flashed through Irene’s head have one thing&nbsp;
in common, they are all her blood relatives.

00:29:05.920 --> 00:29:08.480
When Irene’s mom says “I will always be with you”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:08.480 --> 00:29:12.560
she’s not just talking about her memory. She’s&nbsp;
referring to the supernatural power of the St.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:12.560 --> 00:29:16.720
Lucy bloodline. The power that when combined&nbsp;
with the eyes of St. Lucy, seems to protect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:16.720 --> 00:29:21.960
her from the threat of burnination. Through the&nbsp;
fire and the flames, Sister Irene carries on.

00:29:21.960 --> 00:29:23.600
It’s further suggested shortly after,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:23.600 --> 00:29:26.800
when Irene recalls Father Ridley’s&nbsp;
quip about the Lucy family.

00:29:26.800 --> 00:29:31.520
–[Ridley] Lucy was murdered. Her family escaped.&nbsp;
They were hunted. Scattered across the globe.

00:29:31.520 --> 00:29:36.080
Perhaps the eyes of St. Lucy are not only&nbsp;
an artifact, but also a generational gift&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:36.080 --> 00:29:40.200
allowing those in her bloodline to have psychic&nbsp;
visions? It would certainly seem plausible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:40.200 --> 00:29:44.200
because Lorraine has this gift, and in&nbsp;
The Conjuring 2 and Annabelle Comes Home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:44.200 --> 00:29:47.520
it’s clear that she’s passed it&nbsp;
down to *her* daughter, Judy Warren.

00:29:47.520 --> 00:29:52.040
–[Judy] Mom. Who is that?

00:29:52.040 --> 00:29:56.720
But the battle isn’t over yet. Sister Debra joins Sister Irene in prayer, and in probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:56.720 --> 00:30:01.280
the most French thing that could have possibly&nbsp;
happened, barrels of red wine burst open and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:01.280 --> 00:30:07.480
wash Valak away (!), causing the infernal enemy&nbsp;
to somehow dry up and combust in an epic inferno.

00:30:07.480 --> 00:30:11.440
Frenchie is temporarily able to regain&nbsp;
control of his body, but the evil would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:11.440 --> 00:30:15.120
continue to lie dormant inside of him. But&nbsp;
for the time being, it seemed that Sister&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:15.120 --> 00:30:20.280
Irene had paid back a favor by saving his life&nbsp;
four years after he had done the same for her.

00:30:20.280 --> 00:30:23.360
The two would see each other off&nbsp;
for presumably the final time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:23.360 --> 00:30:27.240
this time, with just a nod, as Frenchie&nbsp;
moves on with his new found-family.

00:30:27.800 --> 00:30:29.120
Yeah, and then that’s just it.

00:30:29.120 --> 00:30:33.840
Sister Irene’s story arc is not a typical final&nbsp;
girl archetype of a girl coming out of her shell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:33.840 --> 00:30:38.240
to kill the villain or overcoming her fear to&nbsp;
escape her stalker. In true Conjuring fashion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:38.240 --> 00:30:41.880
it’s more of a spiritual journey.&nbsp;
She’s been chosen by a higher power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:41.880 --> 00:30:44.480
whether that be God or Cardinal “Bad News” Conroy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:44.480 --> 00:30:48.480
and she’s forced to demonstrate her faith by&nbsp;
taking her vows and believing in her visions.

00:30:48.480 --> 00:30:52.600
My problem is that her entire character arc&nbsp;
is completed in The Nun 1, and character-wise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:52.600 --> 00:30:57.440
nothing really happens with her in The Nun 2. You&nbsp;
could say I was Nun 2 pleased with the sequel.

00:30:57.440 --> 00:31:01.640
The extremely helpful librarian Father Ridley&nbsp;
does more than she does in that movie. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:01.640 --> 00:31:05.800
literally does all the work for her, he solves&nbsp;
the mystery of the Lucy family crest for her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:05.800 --> 00:31:08.880
he explains all the lore to them,&nbsp;
then, when she wants to find the eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:08.880 --> 00:31:11.991
he’s like “I already found them”&nbsp;
and tells her exactly where to go.

00:31:12.040 --> 00:31:15.440
It’s so bizarre. Irene is basically&nbsp;
only relevant in The Nun 2 because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:15.440 --> 00:31:19.320
she was born with St. Lucy’s blood. It’s&nbsp;
not something she earned or struggled for,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:19.320 --> 00:31:22.560
so it feels cheap when that ends up&nbsp;
being what helps her overcome Valak.

00:31:22.560 --> 00:31:26.440
This is what I call a “chosen one” story.&nbsp;
There are two types of chosen one stories:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:26.440 --> 00:31:29.360
the good kind and the bad kind. In&nbsp;
the good kind, the hero is destined&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:29.360 --> 00:31:33.040
to be the only one who can defeat the&nbsp;
villain, but success is not guaranteed.

00:31:33.040 --> 00:31:37.120
For example, in Harry Potter, which also&nbsp;
takes place in a European boarding school,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:37.120 --> 00:31:41.200
a prophecy seems to point to Harry being the only&nbsp;
one with the power to defeat the Dark Lord, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:41.200 --> 00:31:45.520
he still has to mature and form relationships and&nbsp;
overcome adversity by embracing the power of love&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:45.520 --> 00:31:50.120
along the way. His character arc ultimately puts&nbsp;
him in a position where he *could* be the victor.

00:31:50.120 --> 00:31:54.160
The Legend of Zelda: Twilight Princess has a&nbsp;
protagonist referred to as the Hero Chosen by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:54.160 --> 00:31:58.640
the Gods. But that doesn’t make him immune to&nbsp;
death. He has to build trust with companion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:58.640 --> 00:32:02.400
Midna, and learn ancient skills along&nbsp;
the way in order to even have a chance.

00:32:02.400 --> 00:32:05.120
Sister Irene seems to just&nbsp;
be invincible against fire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:05.120 --> 00:32:07.760
because she was born that way.&nbsp;
She didn’t really earn it.

00:32:07.760 --> 00:32:11.960
She’s more like Rey from the Star Wars sequel&nbsp;
trilogy, she’s essentially able to win very early&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:11.960 --> 00:32:16.680
on because of who she is. Again, this is more of a&nbsp;
problem with the second Nun movie than the first.

00:32:16.680 --> 00:32:19.600
If you want to see an example of how this&nbsp;
could have been done a little bit better,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:19.600 --> 00:32:21.320
watch Insidious: The Last Key.

00:32:21.320 --> 00:32:25.680
In that movie, Elise Rainier is a psychic&nbsp;
ghost and demon hunter, just like Sister Irene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:25.680 --> 00:32:29.960
who had almost the exact same problem -- with her&nbsp;
dad not believing or being afraid of her psychic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:29.960 --> 00:32:34.120
abilities and treating her poorly because of it.&nbsp;
Elise lives her life hunting some of the world’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:34.120 --> 00:32:38.600
scariest demons, but none of that compares to&nbsp;
her personal demons with her father. In the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:38.600 --> 00:32:41.680
the antagonist, Keyface, uses her&nbsp;
father’s ghost to confront her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:41.680 --> 00:32:45.360
and she must overcome the familial issues&nbsp;
in order to hunt down her real enemy.

00:32:45.360 --> 00:32:49.680
Valak has the ability to take on any form,&nbsp;
which is why it chooses the Nun form to mock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:49.680 --> 00:32:53.720
the sisters at the Abbey of St. Carta in Nun&nbsp;
1, so it would have made sense for one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:53.720 --> 00:32:57.480
alternate forms to resemble Sister Irene’s&nbsp;
personal demon in her relationship with her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:57.480 --> 00:33:01.680
father in the second movie. You know, instead of&nbsp;
this random goat from the stained glass window.

00:33:01.680 --> 00:33:04.680
If you want to see my full analysis of&nbsp;
Keyface, by the way, that link will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:04.680 --> 00:33:09.040
in the description. But to get a proper grasp on&nbsp;
how everything connects in the Conjuring Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:09.040 --> 00:33:12.160
you’ll want to have your pointer&nbsp;
possess that playlist on the left.

00:33:12.160 --> 00:33:16.480
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new&nbsp;
horrors every week, ring the deathbell for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:16.480 --> 00:33:23.228
all notifications and I’ll see you in&nbsp;
the next one. Assuming we both survive.

